// PORT-PENDING 1039 tests-diagnostic-snapshots: tests/diagnostic_snapshots.rs:1-1754
// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! Snapshot tests for every user-facing diagnostic (invariant I4): errors
//RS //! (tests/ui/*.jet + .stderr) and ownership lints (tests/ui_lint/*.jet +
//RS //! .warn), both driven by the same `UPDATE_EXPECT` snapshot harness.
//RS //!
//RS //! Each flat tests/ui/NAME.jet has a sibling NAME.stderr holding the exact
//RS //! rendered output. A directory fixture uses `run.jet` or legacy `main.jet`
//RS //! plus `stderr`, or
//RS //! `workspace.jet` + tests/ui/NAME.stderr. Each tests/ui_lint/NAME.jet has a
//RS //! sibling NAME.warn.
//RS //! To update after an INTENTIONAL wording change:
//RS //!
//RS //!     JET_UI_FILTER=tests/ui/NAME.jet UPDATE_EXPECT=tests/ui/NAME.jet \
//RS //!       cargo test --test diagnostic_snapshots ui_snapshots
//RS //!
//RS //! A reviewed sweep still exists, but `UPDATE_EXPECT=1` now demands
//RS //! `UPDATE_EXPECT_REASON="<the compiler change that justifies it>"`. Card #2026
//RS //! measured a blanket sweep (6fd88282b) that rewrote 122 fixtures while
//RS //! touching zero crate source: a contract rewrite with no author. The reason
//RS //! names the author.
//RS //!
//RS //! Blessing may add or reword a diagnostic; it may never silently drop one.
//RS //! `write_blessed_snapshot` refuses a write that lowers a fixture's rendered
//RS //! diagnostic count unless `UPDATE_EXPECT_SHRINK=<fixture>` names that exact
//RS //! fixture. 6fd88282b dropped five live `E0209` rows from
//RS //! tests/ui/core_consuming_borrowed_field.stderr that way, and the snapshot
//RS //! then asserted five clones codegen still inserts.
//RS //!
//RS //! Never bless a snapshot you haven't read against the typed diagnostic row.
//RS //! These files are the product: the error messages ARE the language's UX.
//RS 
